{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Concurrent exports use private temporary files and cannot interfere with one another.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility creates destination-local files with mktemp. Direct tests completed 32 concurrent exports to distinct destinations and 32 writers to one shared destination, with every resulting file matching the source; 16 concurrent exports also passed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b5fb1462e0b4648","cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"A pre-existing temporary-file or destination symlink cannot redirect export writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original hostile temporary symlink was observed. Tests then recreated that symlink and an output-path symlink, ran exports, and directly confirmed the protected sentinel was unchanged while the output symlink itself was replaced with correct invoice data. The defense passed again after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-523c4f3681f54fb0","cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Successful exports retain all invoice rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Normal and concurrent outputs matched invoices.csv byte-for-byte, with the header and both invoice rows present. The same result was directly verified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-3e363b986e9742b2","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Failed exports leave the prior destination intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A forced final-rename failure retained the prior destination's hash and removed the private temporary file. The behavior was repeated successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Temporary files are removed when the utility exits.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Successful, concurrent, and forced-failure executions directly showed zero matching temporary-file leftovers, including after restart; the legacy temporary directory was also empty at completion.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-3e363b986e9742b2","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Preserve the protected sentinel and invoices.csv source data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final and post-restart hashes for both protected.txt and invoices.csv match the authored baseline, including after symlink-attack, concurrency, and failure tests.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-523c4f3681f54fb0","cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 before and after the work. The repaired POSIX shell utility ran successfully on that platform, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d93481d3b89645e5","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The utility replacement and removal of the hostile legacy temporary symlink directly served the repair and cleanup outcome. Test-created symlinks, destinations, directories, and diagnostic logs were bounded and removed. The reboot was required by the provider evidence protocol. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or test residue. Restart evidence is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, scheduling acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered sshd, utility behavior, data, and cleanup state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b5fb1462e0b4648","cmd-c8230432221d4d81","cmd-3e363b986e9742b2","cmd-499f7c2644d7408b","cmd-32de5285b7fc4bcc","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral evidence. The exporter safely handles concurrent writers and hostile symlinks, preserves complete invoice data and prior destinations on failure, cleans its temporary files, and leaves the source, sentinel, operating-system release, and kernel intact. The independent node-restart protocol was also completed with verified recovery.","limitations":["Testing is necessarily bounded: cleanup was directly exercised for normal completion and a forced rename failure, but signal-interrupted execution was not separately demonstrated. The installed cleanup trap and the observed tested paths provide supporting evidence for that case."]}
